in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @docs
in @docs/tea
in @docs/design
in @ui
in @nl

# @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study — the concrete @docs/tea
# instance shape for spectral.engineer/case-study/X (Phase F; substrate
# -decl for the FIRST DEPLOYED PAGE).
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23: the first case study to ship is the Fellowship
# stated-vs-enacted Connes distance — a page that takes two @nl
# corpora (the stated charter of a fellowship; the enacted record of
# the same fellowship) and projects their @nl.connes_distance into a
# typed visualisation via @ui's eigenboard instrument. The page
# composes punk-zine perimeter (cover/header/footer) with ND-friendly
# long-form body (Atkinson + Tufte sidenotes) per @docs/design's
# perimeter-loud/body-calm principle.
#
# === What this species declares ===
#
# The typed SHAPE of the first spectral.engineer page as a @docs/tea
# instance: the case_study_model carrier (Model side), the case_study
# _msg sum (Msg side), the cover/body/chrome/toggle/machine-readable
# section layouts (View side), and the init/update/view/subscribe
# actions specialized for the case-study page (Update + View + Sub
# sides). Embeds @ui's eigenboard via subscribe_events; consumes
# @docs/design's tokens via render_palette + render_typography.
#
# === The composition ===
#
# Design tokens (@docs/design palette + typography + section_layout)
# + TEA pattern (@docs/tea model + msg + update + view + cmd + sub)
# + eigenboard instrument (@ui field + subscribe_events bridge)
# + text measurement (@nl corpus + connes_distance + project
# _measurement) = one typed page.
#
# === Forward-promised ===
#
# - Gleam Lustre implementation at Phase G; cascade<gleam, js>
#   delivery; StageFreight content-addressed deployment
# - The actual stated + enacted Fellowship corpora (Phase G data load)
# - URL slug "X" concrete value pending Alex confirmation (fellowship
#   | the-fellowship | fellowships-stated-vs-enacted)
# - CSS print stylesheet (print_friendly = true is substrate claim;
#   discharge at Phase G)
#
# Spec context: shards/docs/tea.mirror (parent species; M/V/U pattern);
#               shards/docs/design.mirror (Phase E tokens this species
#                resolves);
#               shards/docs.mirror (parent family-root; document /
#                rendered_page carriers);
#               shards/ui.mirror (subscribe_events bridge);
#               shards/nl.mirror (corpus / spectral_triple /
#                project_measurement bridge);
#               shards/cascade/code/gleam/js.mirror (the cascade
#                species that delivers this instance to browser);
#               tasks/active/spectral-engineer-case-study-fellowship.md
#                (forward-promised content brief; Phase G).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (case_study_model /
#                       case_study_msg / cover_layout / body_layout /
#                       page_chrome / theme_toggle / machine_metadata
#                       are separate carriers for separate concepts),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (every primitive on this page already exists
#                       at parent altitude; this species is COMPOSITION,
#                       not invention),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; SSR-vs-client and HTTP
#                       data-fetch effects fire at @io, not here).
# Recognition ancestry: #59 kintsugi loop altitude-portable (the
#                       composed bilateral lifts here too — 10th
#                       altitude instance landing today, after
#                       cascade / ui / docs / tea / design / rust-
#                       wasm / ps-npm / gleam-js / gleam-beam);
#                       #93 H4 (labeled<> at page altitude via
#                       rendered_page from @docs);
#                       #95 @cascade family-root (Gleam Lustre
#                       delivery is cascade<gleam, js>);
#                       #96 candidate territory (instrument @ui +
#                       presentation @docs partition at the
#                       deployed-page altitude — third witness).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study.mirror` declares
# `@docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/gleam-lustre
source @arxiv/typography/tufte-2001-visual-display
source @arxiv/web/aipref-content-usage
source @arxiv/web/llms-txt

prism @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study {
  focus case_study
  project layout
  split section
  shift event
  settle render
}

# === §1 Model — case_study state ===
#
# The typed page state for the Fellowship case study. Specializes
# @docs/tea's bare `model = ref` into the concrete carrier the
# page-runtime consumes. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] every named
# concept gets its own carrier; the model is the composition.

# Page identifier: the URL slug. Forward-promised concrete value
# pending Alex confirmation (see hedge 6).
type case_study_id = ref

# Per-section disclosure state. Sections start `closed`; reader opens
# on click; some open by default (the cover, the punctum claim).
type section_state = open | closed

# Theme selection per @docs/design tech toggle (Decision 4):
# `light` = human-light (cream wine-leaked) | `dark` = human-dark or
# tech-dark (wine-cave; tech-dark adds Recursive MONO at 1.0).
type theme_state = light | dark

# Lazy measurement: the @nl.connes_distance between stated and enacted
# corpora is computed on demand (potentially expensive; bounded by
# corpus size and Dirac operator construction). `none` until requested;
# `some(triple)` after measurement_loaded msg fires.
type measurement_state = option(spectral_triple)

# THE LOAD-BEARING MODEL CARRIER. The complete page state at the @docs
# /tea altitude, specialized for this case study. Composes seven typed
# fields:
#
#   id              the URL slug (case_study_id)
#   title           the page title (nl literal: e.g., "The Fellowship")
#   stated_corpus   the charter / stated commitment (@nl corpus)
#   enacted_corpus  the record of what happened (@nl corpus)
#   measurement     lazy Connes distance + spectral triple
#   eigenboard      the @ui field rendering the measurement
#   selected_aside  which sidenote is currently expanded (mobile)
#   theme           current theme_state
#   viewer_state    scroll position + open-section map (for restore)
type case_study_model = ref

# === §2 Msg — page events ===
#
# The typed event sum the runtime dispatches into update_case_study.
# Specializes @docs/tea's bare `msg = ref` into the concrete sum.
# Per Elm: every state transition fires through a typed msg; the sum
# is exhaustive.
#
# Eight constructors at v0.1 (Phase G may add more as interaction
# surfaces; the family-root sum is open by construction at this
# instance altitude):
#
#   measurement_requested(id)     reader clicked "measure"; dispatch
#                                 connes_distance cmd to @io
#   measurement_loaded(triple)    @io returned the result; update
#                                 model and pass triple to eigenboard
#   section_toggled(ref)          reader expanded/collapsed a section
#   aside_opened(ref)             mobile reader tapped a sidenote
#                                 anchor (Tufte collapse-below-900px
#                                 per @docs/design §4)
#   theme_switched(theme_state)   user toggled human <-> tech
#   ui_event_received(ui_event)   bubbled from @ui.subscribe_events;
#                                 mote_clicked / viewer_panned / etc.
#   viewer_panned(ref)            scroll-position update (debounced)
#   page_loaded(case_study_id)    initial mount complete; init cmd
#                                 dispatch finished
type case_study_msg = ref

# === §3 Cover template (F1; punk-zine perimeter) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §4.2: the cover IS the perimeter — display stencil
# face (cover-only; never body), high-contrast Track A palette, Sniffin'
# Glue cut-paste asymmetric register. The bleed_into_body horizontal
# rule IS the threshold between perimeter aggression and body care.
#
# Fields:
#   title                   the case study title (nl literal)
#   subtitle                short framing line (nl literal; one line)
#   image_oid               cover image content-hash (@mirror/store
#                            content-addressed; Phase G load)
#   aggression_register     `high` for this case; punctum hook
#   bleed_into_body         horizontal rule 4px in color_punctum
#                            (the threshold; the visual semicolon)
#
# Composes @docs/design tokens:
#   palette       wine_50 background (light) / wine_950 (dark)
#   typography    Stencil display face for title; Atkinson for subtitle
#   section_layout the broken-grid asymmetric cover layout
#
# Body discharges at Phase G Lustre view function.
type cover_layout = ref

# === §4 Long-form body template (F2; ND-friendly) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §4 (body sizing locked): 18px / 1.7 / 50-75ch /
# Atkinson Hyperlegible Next. NEVER justified; left-aligned. Tufte
# sidenotes in margin >= 900px, collapsed inline below.
#
# Lifts the aside[data-actor] + aside[data-side] + [data-role='claim'] +
# [data-role='evidence'] patterns from systemic.engineering's
# page.gleam:128-134 (named in @docs/design §4 layout).
#
# Fields:
#   column_max_width     50-75ch (ND-friendly column)
#   line_height          1.7 (above 1.5 dyslexia floor)
#   font_size            18px base
#   font_family          atkinson_hyperlegible_next (body face)
#   sidenote_pattern     tufte collapse-below-900px
#   paragraph_spacing    1.5em between paragraphs; no first-line indent
#   heading_rhythm       1.5x scale; no skipped levels
#
# Composes @docs/design tokens:
#   typography_stack    body face + heading face from §3
#   section_layout      body section_layout from §4
#   palette             wine ladder (50/100 light bg; 850/950 dark)
type body_layout = ref

# === §5 Index / nav / footer (F3) ===
#
# Page chrome: top breadcrumb nav, semantic footer, print-friendly
# stylesheet claim. Per @docs/design §4 footer specification: wine_700
# background, wine_300 text, minimal; the page settles here.
#
# Fields:
#   nav              top breadcrumb: Index > Case Studies > Fellowship
#   footer           { license, repo_link, show_me_your_work_v0_2 }
#   print_friendly   substrate claim; CSS @media print at Phase G
#
# Notes:
#   - license = SEL terms URL per @docs/design §6 machine-readability
#   - repo_link = source-of-truth corpus location (for citation)
#   - show_me_your_work_v0_2 = forward-promised per @docs/design H7
#     (visible structure surfacing the spectral triple's H component;
#     defers to v0.2)
type page_chrome = ref

# === §6 Tech toggle (F4) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §5: three rendering configurations, two user-facing
# toggles. Default honors prefers-color-scheme; tech toggle is explicit
# opt-in to wine-cave-in-monospace (Recursive MONO at 1.0). Persistence
# via localStorage `spectral_theme` key.
#
# Fields:
#   default        prefers_color_scheme (system preference resolves)
#   user_override  localStorage persistence (`spectral_theme` key)
#   light          wine_50 + wine_950 + atkinson (cream + near-black)
#   dark           wine_850 + wine_50 + monospace (wine-cave-in-mono
#                  per @docs/design §5 + spectral-engineer-color.md
#                  Decision 9 Matrix-without-dystopia)
#
# Open at v0.1 (forward-promised per @docs/design §5 final block):
#   - Selection highlight color per mode
#   - Cursor blink rate in tech view (respect prefers-reduced-motion)
#   - Mobile toggle UI location
type theme_toggle = ref

# === §7 Machine-readability layer (F5) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §6 + Mara research spectral-engineer-agents.md
# Part 8 synthesis. The corpus position: anti-extraction is NOT
# anti-agent. SEL §3 protects; AIPREF + llms.txt + JSON-LD welcome.
# Single-source-of-truth per Decision 8.
#
# Fields:
#   aipref            { training: allow_with_sel,
#                       inference: allow_with_sel }
#                     per-page Content-Usage header per AIPREF draft
#   robots            no AI-targeted disallow blocks; sitemap reference
#                     (refuse the bifurcation between walled garden
#                      and extraction-target)
#   llms_txt          auto-generated from frontmatter at build time
#                     (title + 1-line summary + URL per piece)
#   llms_full_txt     complete corpus concatenated; nightly refresh
#   json_ld           Article + ScholarlyArticle additionalType;
#                     author "Alex Wolf + Reed (Pack)";
#                     datePublished "2026-06-23";
#                     about "Fellowship stated-vs-enacted Connes
#                            distance"
#
# The agent-facing layer renders identically across all three themes
# (Decision 8: semantic/rendering separation is structural).
type machine_metadata = ref

# === §8 Actions ===
#
# Specializations of @docs/tea's bare init / update / view_of /
# subscribe actions for this case_study. Each carries the purity
# obligation from the parent species. Bodies discharge at Phase G
# Lustre runtime + @io HTTP adapter.

# Construct initial (case_study_model, cmd) pair. The cmd dispatched
# at init MAY load the stated + enacted corpora over HTTP; per @docs
# /tea hedge 4 cmd is a bare ref at v0.1 (typed effect shape forward-
# promised). measurement starts `none`.
init_case_study(id: case_study_id, p: perturbation)
  -> (case_study_model, cmd)
requires init_pure(p)
{ \ }

# Pure (state, msg) -> (new_state, cmd). Per @docs/tea: update_pure
# obligation holds; substrate forecloses hidden side effects.
# Dispatches connes_distance computation cmd on measurement_requested;
# threads ui_event into eigenboard field on ui_event_received;
# persists theme on theme_switched.
update_case_study(
  state: case_study_model,
  m: case_study_msg,
  p: perturbation
) -> (case_study_model, cmd)
requires update_pure(state, m, p)
{ \ }

# Pure model -> view projection. Composes cover_layout + body_layout +
# page_chrome + theme_toggle + machine_metadata + the embedded
# eigenboard @ui field into one rendered view. Per @docs/tea view_pure
# obligation.
view_case_study(state: case_study_model, p: perturbation) -> view
requires view_pure(state, p)
{ \ }

# Pure model -> sub projection. Subscribes to @ui.subscribe_events on
# the eigenboard field for ui_event bubbling (mote_clicked, viewer_
# panned, etc.); each ui_event becomes a case_study_msg via the
# ui_event_received constructor.
subscribe_case_study(state: case_study_model, p: perturbation) -> sub { \ }

# === §9 Composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the @docs/tea/spectral-
# engineer-case-study altitude. Composes purity verdicts from @docs
# /tea + composition verdict from @docs + instrument verdict from @ui
# + design verdict from @docs/design.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined,
# @ui.ui_instrument_coherent, @docs.docs_complete, @docs/tea.tea
# _well_formed, @docs/design.design_complete, @cascade/code/rust/wasm
# .rust_wasm_cascade_well_formed, @cascade/code/purescript/js.ps_npm
# _cascade_well_formed, @cascade/code/gleam/js, @cascade/code/gleam
# /beam — TENTH altitude lift of today's pattern.
#
# Five sub-predicates must hold for the case study to ship:
#   1. init_pure(p)                    @docs/tea
#   2. update_pure(state, m, p)        @docs/tea
#   3. view_pure(state, p)             @docs/tea
#   4. document_well_formed(state, p)  @docs (composition coherence)
#   5. field_well_formed(state, p)     @ui (instrument coherence)
#
# Splinter-pole: all five discharge; page ships.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-predicate fails; deployment blocked at
#   the failing altitude.
# Narcissus-warned: all five discharge but at least one is warned
#   (e.g., document warns deprecated anchor; design warns APCA at
#   lower bound); page ships with audit-flag.
case_study_well_formed(
  state: case_study_model,
  m: case_study_msg,
  p: perturbation
) -> verdict
requires init_pure(p)
requires update_pure(state, m, p)
requires view_pure(state, p)
requires document_well_formed(state, p)
requires field_well_formed(state, p)
{ \ }

# === §10 Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. Measurement loading is async cmd. The connes_distance computation
#    over the stated + enacted Fellowship corpora may take noticeable
#    time (Dirac operator construction is O(n^2) in token count; the
#    Fellowship corpora are bounded but non-trivial). The cmd-effect
#    shape is FORWARD-PROMISED to Phase G — concrete typed effect
#    description (HTTP fetch + worker dispatch) lives at @io adapter
#    altitude per @docs/tea hedge 4.
#
# 2. Eigenboard field construction FROM the measurement is forward-
#    promised at species altitude. The pipeline is:
#      @nl.project_measurement(stated, enacted, p)
#        -> intermediate measurement ref
#      -> field construction (motes = tokens; arcs = Dirac couplings)
#      -> @ui.render(field, p) -> rgba8_buffer
#    The intermediate "measurement-to-field" projection has no
#    substrate primitive yet (Mara recognition surfaces here);
#    Phase G discharges or surfaces a new species shard.
#
# 3. The "show me your work" element per @docs/design §9 H7 is
#    FORWARD-PROMISED to v0.2. This shard declares no carrier for it;
#    a future @docs/work_surface species can specialize content_block
#    once the pattern stabilizes.
#
# 4. SUBSTRATE-DECL ONLY. The Gleam Lustre runtime, the actual page
#    HTML, the CSS bytes, the Webpack/Vite bundling — all Phase G
#    implementation. This shard carries the TYPED SHAPE the
#    implementation discharges against.
#
# 5. Fellowship CONTENT DATA (the actual stated charter text + the
#    enacted record text) is forward-promised to Phase G load. The
#    substrate-decl carries the TYPED SHAPE (case_study_model has
#    stated_corpus + enacted_corpus fields of type @nl.corpus); the
#    concrete corpus bytes load at deployment time from content-
#    addressed storage.
#
# 6. URL slug "X" is a placeholder until Alex confirms (candidates:
#    "fellowship" | "the-fellowship" | "fellowships-stated-vs-
#    enacted"). The substrate carrier case_study_id is concrete;
#    the resolved slug is a Phase G configuration value.
#
# 7. print_friendly = true is a SUBSTRATE CLAIM; the CSS print
#    stylesheet that discharges it lives at Phase G. The substrate-
#    decl admits the claim so the Phase G implementation can fail
#    fast if @media print rendering is skipped.
#
# 8. Recognition #97 candidate (TEA-as-substrate-pattern; surfaced at
#    @docs/tea Phase D) is third-witness territory for this shard.
#    The first deployed @docs/tea instance IS a Pack-ratification
#    surface for #97; if the page ships clean and the discipline
#    holds at Phase G runtime, the candidate promotion-gate opens.
#    Flagged here so Seam can review.
#
# 9. Recognition #96 candidate (instrument-altitude vs presentation-
#    altitude) gets its THIRD witness in this shard: @ui (instrument)
#    composes with @docs (presentation) at this case-study altitude;
#    the embedded eigenboard is instrument-side, the typography body
#    is presentation-side, both compose into one page. If Pack accepts
#    the three-witness pattern (#96 territory: @ui Phase C / @docs
#    Phase D / this shard Phase F), promotion-eligible.
#
# 10. @docs/design tokens are RESOLVED at Phase G via cascade<gleam,
#     js> emitting CSS custom properties. This shard names the
#     section layouts (cover_layout, body_layout, page_chrome,
#     theme_toggle) as separate carriers; the per-token CSS bytes
#     live in the cascade species, not here. Conflating "names the
#     vocabulary" with "emits CSS" would be the form/process error.

out @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study
out case_study_id
out section_state
out theme_state
out measurement_state
out case_study_model
out case_study_msg
out cover_layout
out body_layout
out page_chrome
out theme_toggle
out machine_metadata
out init_case_study
out update_case_study
out view_case_study
out subscribe_case_study
out case_study_well_formed
